OL,3,GNEWSAAgeing playgrounds could face
OL,4,Aclosure
OL,5,
OL,6,FMore than 30 playgrounds could be
OL,7,Fclosed as a council assesses the
OL,8,Fcondition of equipment at the sites.
OL,10,FDurham County Council has identified
OL,11,Fdozens of spots which could be phased
OL,12,Fout or removed as part of its wider
OL,13,Fstrategy for outdoor play.
OL,15,FPlaygrounds, including some in Bishop
OL,16,FAuckland, Durham, Murton, Newton
OL,17,FAycliffe and Spennymoor, have been
OL,18,Fdescribed as being in poor condition or
OL,19,Fconsidered surplus because other
OL,20,Ffacilities are nearby.
OL,23,APub: 17-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
